Rule applied: a PTC more than {{ nmd.rules.last_junction_nt }} nt upstream of the last exon-exon junction is predicted to trigger nonsense-mediated decay; a PTC in the last exon, or within that window, escapes it. The cDNA position recomputed from the exon structure is checked against VEP's before any verdict is issued.
